[#:seon.task{:name "branch-creation-is-serialized-store-wide"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every branch! takes Datahike's store-wide :roster reachability permit (gc_guard.cljc:99, exclusive among roster publishers) for the read-modify-write of :branches; each test member creates a branch. `seon.cluster.registry/branch!` averaged 23 ms serial and 66 ms at six concurrent requests (105 calls). Done when member branch creation does not serialize concurrent requests: batch roster publication per request, or a compare-and-set roster update in the fork, measured by the same N=6 probe."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/branch! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-status-read-pays-a-store-read-for-the-current-source-commit"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.registry/connection-branch-commit-id` for :current-src costs 2.9 ms per call (default 2026-09-28), a third of a warm health report (`seon.cluster.status/snapshot`). Read the branch commit from a value the process already holds, or key it by what changes it (publication); done when a warm status read is under 1 ms."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/connection-branch-commit-id seon.cluster.status/snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/health-page--RESUME.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-retire-branch-error-repeats-in-every-reply"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every eval_clj reply of agent context-refine-2 carried :errors [{:seon.error/operation seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!, :seon.error/message \"Connection has been released.\", :seon.error.occurrence/branch :agent-4beef79d9cf9, :seon.error/signature 759d40be224b...}], a retirement of that agent's own branch (:agent-4beef79d9cf9) the agent never called, shown again in each later reply with a growing occurrence count while its evaluations succeeded (lane context-refine-2, default 795a770c2, 2026-10-08). Done when a retirement's failure is answered to whoever called retire-branch! and recorded once at its main, never repeated in replies whose evaluations did not cause it."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-cluster-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Give `seon.cluster.registry/cluster-branch` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it (`docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`): registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, file a task on the producer naming `seon.cluster.registry/cluster-branch` in its must-read with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/cluster-branch seon.contracts/gaps}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "retiring-a-branch-records-connection-has-been-released"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!` recorded the error \"Connection has been released.\" (layer `:seon.error/normalization`) on default twice on 2026-10-10: on branch `:agent-ff62f12abb61` during agent eval-fixes' `my.test/check` (12:22:53Z), and on `:cluster-default` during root's `my.program/ns-unmap!` (12:29:30Z), signature 759d40be224b. Retiring a branch whose connection another holder already released should answer that the connection is gone, not record an error. Done when retirement after release records nothing and a regression retires a branch whose connection was released first."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fork-writes-no-transaction-on-its-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase H8 of hybrid-start-a-flow.md, last and measured first. The attempt carries `:seon.task.attempt/fork-point` (a commit id, never t, which a fork repeats), and the merge base of an attempt's branch is that commit through Datahike lineage, so `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` stops writing the fork entity (`seon.cluster.registry/branch-fork-entity`) on the new branch and a fork is `datahike.api/branch!` alone (17 ms pointer against 40-53 ms today). Measure first who reads :seon.branch/base-t (`seon.cluster.registry/fork-of`, `seon.cluster.registry/advanced-base-t`, `seon.cluster.source/compare-branch`); more than one owner's afternoon keeps the entity and this task waits. Proofs: this test (the new branch's head commit is the fork point; fork under 25 ms through `seon.profile/measure`); seon.cluster.source-test/the-merge-base-of-an-attempt-is-its-fork-point-commit (the diff since it equals today's diff since :seon.branch/base-t on the two-leaf fixture). Files: src/seon/cluster/registry.clj, src/seon/cluster/source.clj, src/seon/task.clj, test/seon/cluster/registry_test.clj, test/seon/cluster/source_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/fork! seon.cluster.registry/branch-fork-entity seon.cluster.registry/fork-of seon.cluster.source/compare-branch datahike.api/branch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-start-a-flow.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fork-from-a-test-member-retains-its-base-commit"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.registry/fork!` must derive a non-nil base commit when `my.agent/create-branch!` forks from a test member's captured commit. `my.agent-test/retiring-a-branch-this-process-still-connects-is-refused-as-a-value` errors before retirement: `seon.cluster.registry/branch!` receives :seon.store/branch :base/held-lane and :seon.cluster.registry/from nil. The member's overlay must hold the base commit `seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id` reads."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/fork! seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id seon.cluster.registry/branch! my.agent/create-branch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/sol-retire-connection.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-merged-base-older-than-the-window-survives-collection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase U4 of hybrid-push.md (after U0; platform slice with a fork bump, --test). An auto-merge's base (the merge request's moving merge base) is the retained commit :seon.task.attempt/merged names (and before the first auto-merge the attempt's :seon.task.attempt/fork), opened with `datahike.api/commit-as-db`; `datahike.gc/reachable-in-branch` keeps an ancestor only while every newer commit on its path is inside :seon.config.db/snapshot-window-ms, so a merged base followed by an hour of evaluations would be swept and the next auto-merge would have no base (no-history attributes count and last-at have no as-of). Owner approved option A: the fork's `datahike.gc/gc-storage!` gains :datahike.gc/roots, commit ids walked exactly as heads are (the head lookup is reachable-in-branch's only branch-specific line; no second walker); `seon.cluster.registry/collect-and-inventory!` derives them from main's merged and fork values of roster branches before marking. Nothing is written per auto-merge (no force-branch! ref, 18 ms each). Proofs: this test (collect! with a 0 ms window after untracked commits on the branch: the merged base and the predecessor's fork commit still open with commit-as-db and the next auto-merge's delta is exact); the fork's kaocha :clj-pss suite green in reference-code/datahike. Files: reference-code/datahike (gc.cljc), src/seon/cluster/registry.clj, test/seon/cluster/registry_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/collect! seon.cluster.registry/retention-cutoff seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id datahike.api/gc-storage datahike.api/commit-as-db}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-push.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/plan-push-opus.md"}}]
